So the thing about b/p is that it doesn't stop you from absorbing the calories. Typically, you'll absorb most if not all of the calories from a binge. What's more, binge foods are typically highly-processed and therefore much easier to absorb. Basically, calories become more and more easily absorbable the more processed the food is. I used to be addicted to laxatives and I did lose a lot of weight but I was also restricting my calorie intake to be super low.

&amp;#x200B;

It was also  NOT worth it. Due to my past laxative addition I am constantly dehydrated and I have a recurring UTI. It is totally bunk.
